// <p><strong>Dos:</strong></p>

// <p>1. Respect the Queue: When waiting for an elevator, form a line and wait your turn. <strong>Teknix Elevators</strong>,<strong> </strong>manufacturers in India<strong> </strong>design their systems to handle a certain capacity, and crowding the entrance only slows down the process for everyone.</p>

// <p>2. Hold the Door: If you see someone rushing to catch the elevator, hold the door open for them. It&#39;s a simple gesture of courtesy that can make a big difference in someone&#39;s day.</p>

// <p>3. Allow Exiting Passengers First: When the elevator arrives at your floor, step aside and allow those inside to exit before entering. This helps maintain a smooth flow of traffic and prevents congestion.</p>

// <p>4. Be Mindful of Space: Once inside the elevator, move towards the back to make room for others entering. Avoid crowding around the doors, as this can make it difficult for people to get on and off.</p>

// <p>5. Use Inside Voices: Elevators can be echoey spaces, so be mindful of the noise level of your conversations and avoid speaking loudly, especially in <strong>Residential elevators in Hyderabad </strong>where neighbors might be close by.</p>

// <p>6. Respect Personal Space: While it&#39;s common to share an elevator with strangers, be mindful of personal space boundaries. Avoid standing too close to others, especially in crowded elevators.</p>

